      "title": "Allies did not warn Kyiv of Russian ballistic missile strikes, says Zelenskyy",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/13/allies-did-not-warn-kyiv-of-russian-ballistic-missile-strikes-says-zelenskyy",
      "description": "<p>Ukrainian president’s comments on ‘particularly vile’ strikes come after US threatened to halt intelligence sharing</p><p>Ukraine received no early warning from its partners about a Russian ballistic missile strike on Kyiv in which five missiles hit civilian infrastructure, Volodymyr Zelenskyy said on Tuesday.</p><p>The Ukrainian president <a href=\"https://x.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/2109938658576887917\">described the attack on Monday</a> as “particularly vile”. He emphasised that receiving intelligence from Ukraine’s western allies “helps saves lives, and this is one of the most critical issues”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/13/allies-did-not-warn-kyiv-of-russian-ballistic-missile-strikes-says-zelenskyy\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-13T17:17:13"
    },
    {
      "title": "U.S. Still Shares Intelligence With Ukraine, Both Say, Amid Fears It Could Stop",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/13/world/europe/ukraine-trump-intelligence.html",
      "description": "President Volodymyr Zelensky said Kyiv had received no early warning of a Russian missile attack, after an apparent U.S. threat to halt intelligence sharing, but officials say the sharing continues.",
